exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Change the tags, metadata or postings of an existing transaction.

Find the transaction by ID, or by --find ACCOUNT DATE [AMOUNT]. Flags before the first --add, --set or --remove change the transaction; flags after one change that posting, until the next. A --set changes only what it names, and postings no flag names are kept unchanged.

Usage: borrow-checker transaction edit [OPTIONS] [ID]

Arguments:
  [ID]
          Transaction ID. Give this, or --find.

Options:
      --json
          Emit machine-readable JSON instead of human-readable output

          [env: BC_JSON=]

      --db-path <DB_PATH>
          Path to the SQLite database file.

          Overrides the `db_path` config file setting and the platform default. The `BC_DB_PATH` environment variable is also honoured via the config layer rather than directly by this flag.

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity.

          Pass once for info (`-v`), twice for debug (`-vv`), three times for trace (`-vvv`). Use `RUST_LOG` for fine-grained per-crate control.

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease log verbosity.

          Pass once for error-only output (`-q`). Use `RUST_LOG` for fine-grained per-crate control.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Transaction and posting flags:
      --find <ACCOUNT> <DATE> [AMOUNT]
          Find the transaction by a posting on exactly ACCOUNT dated DATE, adding its signed AMOUNT when several match.

      --add <ACCOUNT> [AMOUNT] [COMMODITY]
          Open a new posting on ACCOUNT (path or ID). Without AMOUNT and COMMODITY its amount is elided. Posting flags after it apply to it.

      --set <POSTING> [AMOUNT] [COMMODITY]
          Change a stored posting: a posting ID, an account, or an account with its amount. Posting flags after it say what changes; the rest is kept.

      --remove <POSTING> [AMOUNT] [COMMODITY]
          Remove a stored posting, named as for --set.

      --meta <KEY=VALUE>
          Metadata entry for the transaction, or for the posting it follows. Repeat for several; a key may repeat.

      --clear-meta <KEY>
          Remove every entry under KEY from the transaction, or from the posting it follows.

      --tag <TAG>
          Tag the transaction, or the posting it follows. TAG is an ID or a path; a missing path is created.

      --untag <TAG>
          Remove a tag from the transaction, or from the posting it follows.

      --account <ACCOUNT>
          Move the posting this --set names to ACCOUNT.

      --amount <AMOUNT> <COMMODITY>
          Replace the amount of the posting this --set names.

      --cost <AMOUNT> <COMMODITY>
          Per-unit cost basis of the posting it follows.

      --total-cost <AMOUNT> <COMMODITY>
          Total cost basis of the posting it follows.

      --lot-date <DATE>
          Lot date of the posting's cost.

      --lot-label <LABEL>
          Lot label of the posting's cost.

      --no-cost
          Clear the cost of the posting this --set names.

      --price <AMOUNT> <COMMODITY>
          Per-unit price of the posting it follows.

      --total-price <AMOUNT> <COMMODITY>
          Total price of the posting it follows.

      --no-price
          Clear the price of the posting this --set names.

      --spread <FROM> <UNTIL>
          Accrue the posting it follows over FROM..=UNTIL.

      --no-spread
          Clear the spread of the posting this --set names.
